# Curated artefact -- Phase 4, QHV twin leg, first execution on the Orin (2026-09-08).
# RESULT: HANG. QEMU 6.2.0 (Ubuntu 22.04 stock), virtio-blk only. The QHV host boots through
# GICv3 ITS, slogger2, PCI, devb-virtio, file-system mount, then stops after
# "random: Could not initialize entropy. [random.c(406)]". Serial log is 419 bytes at 300 s,
# 600 s and after 12 min (three separate runs) -- a deterministic hang, not slowness.
# The line that never arrives is "Unable to access /dev/random", the 5-second timeout message
# of the "waitfor /dev/random" that follows "random ..." in the image's startup.sh (line 40).
# ATTRIBUTED CAUSE (2026-09-09, see docs/findings.md): the QEMU 6.2 *version*, not the host.
# Evidence: with the rng correctly presented the hang moves to the NEXT timeout-wait (io-sock
# start); the same image under QEMU 11.1.0 boots to the guest banner on this same board with
# and without rng (q111-* logs). MECHANISM, hypothesised and NOT verified: v6.2.0's
# hw/arm/virt.c has no NS-EL2 virtual-timer IRQ wiring (added in QEMU 9.0, 1ec896fe7c) and a
# VHE hypervisor's CNTV_* timers are CNTHV_*; target/arm also gained 5709038aa8 ("Don't apply
# CNTVOFF_EL2 for EL2_VIRT timer", QEMU 10.0). Not bisected. A "-machine virt-8.2" run on
# QEMU 11 booting proves nothing either way: that compat flag only hides the IRQ from the
# device tree and leaves the wiring, so it is not a discriminator. NOT a host finding: the same
# image on the Windows host ran QEMU 11.0.50 and passed.
# host ran QEMU 11.0.50 and passed.
# QEMU args (identical to scripts/launch-qhv-tcg.ps1 / scripts/orin/launch-qhv-on-orin-tcg.sh
# at the time): -machine virt,virtualization=on,gic-version=3 -cpu max -accel tcg -smp 2 -m 2G
#   -drive file=disk-qemu,if=none,id=drv0,format=raw -device virtio-blk-device,drive=drv0
#   [-netdev user,id=n0 -device virtio-net-device,netdev=n0 -object rng-builtin,id=rng0
#    -device virtio-rng-device,rng=rng0]   <- only where the header says rng=slot3
#   -kernel ifs.bin -serial file:<log> -display none -no-reboot
# Images: ifs.bin b2d875057f25a4cbda69966e553629d445cfa44af62cf4c5e121442c9782300a,
#         disk-qemu c71b9499353ca4b1d2c4bffbdebbc509bb12492d86cfb6e07e22d79451b7cdfe
#         (SHA-256 at copy time, verified on the Orin with sha256sum -c; NOTE the raw disk
#          mutates on every boot without -snapshot, which these runs did not use).
# Host: Jetson Orin Nano, L4T 5.15.148-tegra, Cortex-A78AE (CPU part 0xd42), 6 cores, 8 GB.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

